{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1159754-dominate-iv-versus-theban-sorcery","id":1159754,"title":"Dominate IV versus Theban Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-17T02:26:30-08:00","id":1159754,"title":"Dominate IV versus Theban Sorcery","content":"As the title says, if a Kindred uses Dominate IV on another one to play with his memories, can the second Kindred confess under the effect of Theban Sorcery (Liars Plague) even if the initial thought is altered or surpressed?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T02:50:32-08:00","id":1159756,"title":"","content":"Clash of wills. As usual when its a power vs a power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T03:27:59-08:00","id":1159763,"title":"","content":"Since the subject is convinced to saying the truth I would say no. The Liar's Plague wouldn't activate.<br /> <br /> In any case, even if you, as a storyteller, decide to let Liar's Plague activate, it shouldn't be a Clash of Will according to me, because if you fallow this way you are interpreting Liar's Plague something that act as a divination not just a punishment for a lair and modifying the memory is not actually hide a fact, just the way how the subject remember it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T04:06:07-08:00","id":1159770,"title":"","content":"I agree with Marcus, if Lier's Plague can pick up on mistakes then you could cast it on someone and ask them a yes/no question they have no way to know the answer to and learn anything through process of elimination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T05:33:22-08:00","id":1159792,"title":"","content":"Liars plague is surely not working as a divination rod vs facts and fiction, e.g. the believes of the victim that he/she thinks are true. <br /> If you really believe the earth is flat and under the spell, asked if the earth is flat, it doesn't go off even though it's pretty ball-shaped.<br /> <br /> However, if a memory is changed of a particular event or belief with dominate and it's opposed to what the character used to perceive to be true, the Liars Plague should trigger a clash of wills against the dominate. If it wins, it goes of, if it looses, nothing happens and the &quot;lie&quot; is told as it would have been &quot;true&quot;, cus that's what the character believes. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T12:20:13-08:00","id":1159961,"title":"","content":"Fair interpretation, would you roll clash per casting or per question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T16:00:11-08:00","id":1160032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1159754-dominate-iv-versus-theban-sorcery?p=1159961#post1159961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair interpretation, would you roll clash per casting or per question?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Per casting. If the power wins, it wins.<br /> Like you have proven the power level between these individuals for now, in this scene.<br /> Same thing with Auspex Vs Obfuscate for example. You wouldn't get a new roll if the obfuscated one gets behind a curtain and comes forth a few times in the same scene.","signature":"","